   "text": {
    "L1": "For large products, split off the zeros first.",
    "L2": "Multiply the non-zero parts, then attach every zero you removed.",
    "L3": "For 6,000 × 50, multiply 6 × 5 to get 30.",
    "L4": "There are four removed zeros, so the answer is 3,00,000.",
    "L5": "A zero made by the non-zero multiplication still counts. So the zero in 5 × 4 = 20 must stay.",
    "L6": "For a quick estimate, round each number before multiplying: 4,890 × 312 becomes 5,000 × 300, or about 15,00,000.",
    "L7": "Multiplying by 10 shifts every digit one place left. Use the estimate to check the size of an answer."
   },
